# /blog relaunched 2026-07-27 (real routes, real content, was unrouted
# placeholder before that -- see the git history for the no-store block
# this replaces, kept the /blog was unrouted... incident stale for
# reference). Same per-route 300s edge-cache pattern as the routes above,
# now that /blog/ and its articles are real, actively-served pages rather
# than an unrouted path silently inheriting CF's 7-day default.
#
# NOT a /blog/* wildcard, deliberately: CF Pages _headers rules CONCATENATE
# across overlapping patterns rather than "most specific wins" (verified
# empirically this session, see the dead-slug block below) -- a wildcard
# no-store rule here would concatenate onto these specific routes' 300s
# rule rather than being overridden by it, silently defeating caching for
# every article again. Both slash and bare forms listed per route, same
# reason as the dead-slug block below (verified: Cloudflare does not 301
# the bare form to the slash form on this site).
#
# MAINTENANCE: every new article this pipeline publishes needs its own
# pair of lines added here at merge/publish time -- there is no wildcard
# catching new articles automatically, on purpose (see above). An
# unlisted /blog/* path (a removed article, a typo, an old bookmark)
# falls through to CF's default HTML caching rather than this explicit
# 300s pattern -- a real but much lower-severity residual risk than the
# original incident (a live article's stale content persisting), not
# solved here; revisit if it ever actually causes a problem.
/blog/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300, must-revalidate
/blog
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300, must-revalidate
